[2026-09-22 02:54:19] REQ 260922024953-40 START backend=Ollama model=nemotron-3-super:cloud msgs=80 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_heo0sz1b","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/census-window.sh | ssh -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/continuo_known_hosts root@10.66.0.5 'bash -s' 2026-09-22 continuo"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[02:54:10] == census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-22 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\nno journald lines for continuo in window (clean or unit not logging)\n\n[t+04:17/60:00 c35/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_r55rmu28","function":{"index":0,"name":"write_subtask","arguments":{"path":"failure-reduction/gptel-context-quadratic-cost/fix-overlay-removal/implementation","content":"Implement fix for quadratic cost in gptel-context-remove:\n\nThe current implementation has quadratic complexity when removing multiple contexts from the same buffer because:\n1. For each context removal, it scans through all overlays in that buffer to check if any remain\n2. This results in O(n^2) behavior when removing n contexts\n\nFix approach:\n- Instead of checking for remaining overlays after each removal, defer the emptiness check\n- Or use a more efficient data structure to track overlay count per buffer\n- Or simply remove the check if it's not critical for correctness\n\nLooking at the code, the check seems to be setting the alist entry to nil when no overlays remain. This is likely for memory efficiency - to clean up empty context lists.\n\nBetter approach:\n1. Remove the overlay as before\n2. Decrement a counter of overlays for that buffer (maintain this counter in add/remove operations)\n3. Only when counter reaches zero, set the alist entry to nil\n\nOr simpler: since we're already iterating to remove the specific overlay, we could collect all overlays to remove first, then do a single pass to update the alist.\n\nImplementation plan:\n1. For the overlayp context case: remove overlay, then check if buffer's overlay list is empty (but do this efficiently)\n2. For bufferp context: remove all overlays for that buffer, then set alist entry to nil\n3. For stringp context (file/directory): similar to buffer case\n4. For region-active-p: remove all overlays in region, then check affected buffers for emptiness\n5. For anything at point: same as overlayp case\n\nThe key is to avoid repeatedly scanning the same overlay list.\n\nLet me implement a version that:\n- Buffers the overlays to check for emptiness\n- Or maintains a count\n- Or does batch processing"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[02:54:17] Subtask written: failure-reduction/gptel-context-quadratic-cost/fix-overlay-removal/implementation\n[t+04:24/60:00 c36/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_62u568ug","function":{"index":0,"name":"find","arguments":{"path":"/root/i.ar","name":"gptel-context.el"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[02:54:19] <tool_call_error>\nUnknown tool 'find'. Check the tool name and use one of the available tools.\n</tool_call_error>\n[t+04:26/60:00 c37/300]"}]
