[2026-09-22 03:17:18] REQ 260922031507-21 START backend=Ollama model=nemotron-3-super:cloud msgs=42 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_54walqtg","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{"path":"failure-reduction/gptel-context-quadratic-cost/fix-overlay-removal"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[03:17:11] === description ===\nFix quadratic cost in gptel-context-remove by avoiding repeated overlay list traversal when clearing many contexts from same buffer.\n\n=== implementation ===\nImplement fix for quadratic cost in gptel-context-remove:\n\nThe current implementation has quadratic complexity when removing multiple contexts from the same buffer because:\n1. For each context removal, it scans through all overlays in that buffer to check if any remain\n2. This results in O(n^2) behavior when removing n contexts\n\nFix approach:\n- Instead of checking for remaining overlays after each removal, defer the emptiness check\n- Or use a more efficient data structure to track overlay count per buffer\n- Or simply remove the check if it's not critical for correctness\n\nLooking at the code, the check seems to be setting the alist entry to nil when no overlays remain. This is likely for memory efficiency - to clean up empty context lists.\n\nBetter approach:\n1. Remove the overlay as before\n2. Decrement a counter of overlays for that buffer (maintain this counter in add/remove operations)\n3. Only when counter reaches zero, set the alist entry to nil\n\nOr simpler: since we're already iterating to remove the specific overlay, we could collect all overlays to remove first, then do a single pass to update the alist.\n\nImplementation plan:\n1. For the overlayp context case: remove overlay, then check if buffer's overlay list is empty (but do this efficiently)\n2. For bufferp context: remove all overlays for that buffer, then set alist entry to nil\n3. For stringp context (file/directory): similar to buffer case\n4. For region-active-p: remove all overlays in region, then check affected buffers for emptiness\n5. For anything at point: same as overlayp case\n\nThe key is to avoid repeatedly scanning the same overlay list.\n\nLet me implement a version that:\n- Buffers the overlays to check for emptiness\n- Or maintains a count\n- Or does batch processing\n[t+02:03/60:00 c18/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_eb9fos75","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"find /root -name \"gptel-context.el\" 2>/dev/null"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[03:17:16] /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/perm-experiment/i.ar/emacs.d/elpa/gptel-20260826.2228/gptel-context.el\n/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/perm-experiment/gptel/gptel-context.el\n/root/.emacs.d/elpa/gptel-20260826.2228/gptel-context.el\n/root/.emacs.d/gptel-fork/gptel-context.el\n/root/i.ar/emacs.d/elpa/gptel-20260826.2228/gptel-context.el\n\n[t+02:09/60:00 c19/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_3x9nwl6e","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/.emacs.d/gptel-fork/gptel-context.el"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[03:17:18] ;;; gptel-context.el --- Context aggregator for gptel  -*- lexical-binding: t; -*-\n\n;; Copyright (C) 2023-2026  Karthik Chikmagalur\n\n;; Author: daedsidog <contact@daedsidog.com>\n;; Keywords: convenience, buffers\n\n;; SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later\n\n;; This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify\n;; it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by\n;; the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or\n;; (at your option) any later version.\n\n;; This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,\n;; but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of\n;; MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the\n;; GNU General Public License for