or ctx in contexts do (delete-overlay ctx))))\n   (t                                   ;Anything at point\n    (when-let* ((ctx (gptel-context--at-point)))\n      (delete-overlay ctx)))))\n\n(defun gptel-context-remove-all (&optional verbose)\n\n[t+05:15/60:00 c39/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_skxyky1g","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/THREADS.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[09:23:51] * THREADS\nNotices from continuo's wandering (codebase-only, D-017).\nEach notice is a one-line observation that may become a thread.\nAppend, never edit in place. Format:\n  - [YYYY-MM-DD] <notice> (<file/where>)\n- [2026-09-17] Test suite warning: usage log write failed due to missing iar--current-project-name (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-17] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el has a syntax error in the let-binding for fork-path (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-18] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el has a syntax error in the let-binding for fork-path (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-18] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el fails due to missing iar--current-project-name (need to load iar-agent-utils.el) (test-loop-chain.el)\n* [2026-09-18 03:27:15] Fixed test-loop-chain.el: added proper test environment setup (IAR_PROJECT, paths, require iar-agent-utils) to avoid usage log warning about iar--current-project-name being void.\n- [2026-09-18] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el has a syntax error in the let-binding for fork-path (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-18] Fixed lexical-binding warning in test-loop-chain.el, test suite passes (16/16). (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n* 2026-09-18 -- Fixed lexical-binding warnings in test files (13 files) to eliminate test suite warnings.\n- [2026-09-18] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el now passes (16/16) and lexical-binding warnings fixed. (emacs.d/test/te